---
source: crates/tk/tests/scenarios.rs
expression: "p.run(&format!(\"{command} --help\"))"
---
Apply pending Mutations through the configured Remote

Usage: tk sync [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  log  Inspect pending, failed, applying, skipped, cancelled, and abandoned Mutations

Options:
      --skip <MUTATION-ID>
          Mark one failed Mutation skipped before running sync.
          
          Skipping a failed close relinquishes it rather than bypassing it: the Item returns to open and loses its Closing Reason, Dependencies it resolved as their Blocking Item become unresolved, and an accepted Ticket becomes selectable by `tk next` again.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
